# Embedded Tomcat 10.1.55 container-auth CVEs, all fixed upstream in 10.1.58 —
# which is tagged but NOT on Maven Central yet (as of 2026-09-03 the newest
# published 10.1.x IS 10.1.55, so the fix cannot be consumed). The release gate
# would otherwise block every deploy on an unavailable artifact.
#
# Why waiving is defensible here: the app authenticates exclusively through
# Spring Security's OAuth2 resource server (Keycloak JWTs). Tomcat security
# constraints, FORM auth and DIGEST auth — the vehicles of all three CVEs — are
# unused. The Trivy SARIF lane still reports them in code scanning.
#
# DELETE this file and set tomcat.version to 10.1.58+ the moment Central has it
# (see the ext block in build.gradle).
CVE-2026-65182
CVE-2026-65905
CVE-2026-68525
